---
// apps/demo-site/src/components/landing/BentoFeatures.astro
// What Inti adds, as a list of rows. Generative UI and the MCP server have
// their own section (AIPlaygroundSection), so they are not repeated here.
---

<section id="features" class="field field--red">
  <div class="dome" data-scroll></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="h-pair" data-scroll>
      <span class="h-display drift-l">What Inti adds to an Astro site.</span>
      <span class="h-serif drift-r">Without touching your CMS database.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="lede">Inti is a thin, lightweight layer between your Astro frontend and the content you already have.</p>

    <div class="feat-list">
      <article class="feat">
        <h3>Inline editing with real write-back</h3>
        <div>
          <p>
            Double-click any text or heading on your Astro page, type the new content and press Enter. Inti updates the view at once and writes the change to WordPress ACF, Kitsuden rows, Strapi dynamic zones or Keystatic files. If the save fails, the text on screen reverts.
          </p>
          <div class="feat-tags">
            <span class="chip">Optimistic UI</span>
            <span class="chip">Astro Server Action: <span class="mono">inti.updateBlockField</span></span>
            <span class="chip">Reverts if the save fails</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feat">
        <h3>Visual page composer</h3>
        <div>
          <p>
            Add, duplicate, reorder and configure. Every block gets a toolbar with an auto-generated properties panel. Developers define the vocabulary in Astro code; editors compose freely without breaking the CSS.
          </p>
          <div class="feat-tags"><span class="chip">Drag &amp; drop reordering</span></div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feat">
        <h3>Personalization without JS</h3>
        <div>
          <p>
            Create content variants per audience (<code class="kbd-code">device:mobile</code>, country, preferences). Everything resolves on the Astro server, with no extra weight in the client bundle and a control group for metrics.
          </p>
          <div class="feat-tags"><span class="chip">Zero client-side JavaScript</span></div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feat">
        <h3>Keep the SEO your client already set up</h3>
        <div>
          <p>
            Inti automatically reads metadata from the most popular WordPress plugins (<strong>Yoast, RankMath, AIOSEO or SEOPress</strong>) and from Strapi SEO components, normalizing it into a single <code class="kbd-code">page.seo</code> object. The <code class="kbd-code">&lt;IntiSeo&gt;</code> and <code class="kbd-code">&lt;IntiStructuredData&gt;</code> components render canonical tags, Open Graph and Schema.org JSON-LD graphs natively on the server.
          </p>
          <div class="feat-tags">
            <span class="chip">Yoast / RankMath</span>
            <span class="chip">JSON-LD Graph</span>
            <span class="chip">Sitemap with lastmod</span>
            <span class="chip">llms.txt</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feat">
        <h3>Cloudflare &amp; edge ready</h3>
        <div>
          <p>
            With the optional <code class="kbd-code">@intijs/cloudflare</code> package: D1 for content and experiments, Durable Objects for realtime and limits, R2 for media, and Workers AI.
          </p>
          <div class="feat-tags"><span class="chip">Optional: Inti does not depend on Cloudflare</span></div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
